  "description": "Recurring 2-3 cell glyph combinations from the Stone Story RPG ASCII-art tutorials, stored as cell offsets plus codepoints. \"Learning ASCII art is about learning these combinations\" and \"what are the permutations of those symbols in two dimensions on the grid\" (o5v-NS9o4yc 27:56-28:20); \"there are certain combinations of glyphs that always come up\" (5sFVVQcUWVE 11:55). Mirroring these is named as the exercise itself (o5v-NS9o4yc 31:12-31:40).",
  "owner": "Reviewed source data for scripts/glyph_families_viewer.py --mode combo and scripts/compile_native_terminal_atlas.py. The compiler preserves native IDs, relative offsets and mirrors in authored_glyph_vocabulary.glslinc. Generated availability is not runtime motif admission.",
  "mirror_rule": "A combination's horizontal mirror reflects cell columns (col -> cols-1-col, row unchanged) and maps each codepoint through glyph_audit.find_mirror. A codepoint with no find_mirror partner is horizontally symmetric in the font raster and is carried through unchanged (cp_source: identity).",
  "cell_px": 16,
  "font": "assets/fonts/unifont-17.0.04.otf",
